 "census_labelling_defect": "The census in this artifact mislabels ownership: `ps -eo user` truncates the login name to eight characters plus '+', so every process of this user was filed under 'other'. The 3168% recorded as other_cpu_percent was in fact this user's own jobs, all at nice 19. The measurement conditions were nonetheless the intended ones and were verified directly at the time: driver at nice 0, every other job of this user at nice 19, and the GPU held exclusively with the only other compute process paused. The throughput numbers stand; the ownership breakdown in census_before/census_after does not. Fixed in scripts/backend_crossover.py."
